// The words the factory's parts pass to each other. One file, because an
// enum can only name types declared in its own file (finding 29).
//
// DRAFT 2 (2026-11-28, from the user's answers at 10:32). Nothing here is
// built yet; CHOICE TO CONFIRM (Fn) marks what the user has not decided.

// ---- Git: what goes in and comes out.

// A commit of the repository. Opaque: in code, its hash.
subject record Revision { .. }
// A folder of the repository, from its root: where the model is (the
// mitra.toml), and where the code is built (the Cargo.toml).
subject record Root { .. }
// A request: one revision, the model's root and the build's root. The
// input is approved before it reaches the factory (user, answer 6).
subject record Request { at: Revision, model: Root, build: Root }
// What the factory hands back: a branch of commits starting from the
// request's revision, and the report to judge it on. Merging it is done
// outside the factory.
subject record Branch { .. }
subject record Delivery { branch: Branch, report: Report }

// ---- What Mitra and the tests read.

// A Mitra model: the .mitra files under the model's root.
subject record Model { .. }
// The code: the files under the build's root, the model aside.
subject record Tree { .. }
// What changed between two models (from nothing, on a first shot).
subject record ModelDiff { .. }

// Mitra's four verdicts, counted over the model's ensures.
subject record Tally { explained: integer, assumed: integer, contradicted: integer, unsupported: integer }
// Mitra's reasons when `check` refuses a model, and the weakest links when
// `blame` runs: text the coding harness reads in the next brief.
subject record Diagnostics { .. }

// Language is a setting; Rust first (answer 3). More cases later.
subject enum Language { Rust }
// All kinds of tests later; unit tests first (answer 3).
subject enum Capability { Unit }
// One run of the capabilities switched on. A build that fails counts as
// a failure: it is fed back to the harness like a failing test.
subject record TestReport { run: integer, failed: integer, said: Diagnostics }

// ---- The coding harness.

// The fake is scripted by tests, so the factory's tests never need
// inference; opencode is the real one, open source (answer 1).
subject enum CoderKind { Fake, OpenCode }
// What the harness is told: made from the brief in the settings (answer
// 8), the model, and what the last round got wrong. Opaque text.
subject record Brief { .. }
// Text the factory keeps for whoever judges the output: the harness's
// reasoning, the factory's own log.
subject record Log { .. }
// The settings that bound a run: how deep it goes and what it may spend
// (answers 2 and 4). Each one stops the run when reached.
subject record Budget { rounds: integer, tokens: integer, seconds: integer }
// The settings that say when a run has succeeded (answer 2). CHOICE TO
// CONFIRM (F5): one switch for now, whether assumed promises are accepted.
subject record Goal { accept_assumed: bool }
// What one round cost.
subject record Spent { tokens: integer, seconds: integer }
// One round of the harness: the code it leaves, what it cost, and why it
// did what it did.
subject record Round { tree: Tree, spent: Spent, reasoning: Log }

// ---- How a run ends.

// Failures inference cannot fix: they stop the run (answer 4). A failing
// test or build is not one of them: it goes back to the harness.
subject enum Failure { Coder, Git, ModelRefused }
subject enum Stop {
    Done,          // the Judge's condition is met
    OutOfBudget,   // rounds, tokens or time used up
    Failed(Failure)
}

// ---- The report.

// What the request was, by comparing the model at the revision with the
// model the code there was last made for (answer 7).
subject enum Kind { FirstShot, RepeatShot, ChangeRequest }
// What the report points out for the judge of the output (answer 7). All
// are allowed; none stops the run. CHOICE TO CONFIRM (F6): these four.
subject enum Remark {
    OldModelHolds,       // the old model still holds on the new code: did the tests grow?
    OldModelBroken,      // the old model no longer holds: the new one asks for something else
    NewModelHeldBefore,  // the new model held on the old code: perhaps only words changed
    TestsNotGrown        // a change request with no more tests than before
}
// The reviews that come with the output. QUESTION: written by whom.
subject record Reviews { .. }
subject record Report {
    kind: Kind,
    stop: Stop,
    rounds: integer,
    spent: Spent,
    tally: Tally,          // the model at the revision, on the delivered code
    tests: TestReport,
    model_change: ModelDiff,
    remarks: [Remark],
    reasoning: Log,        // the harness's, round by round
    log: Log,              // the factory's, for debugging it
    reviews: Reviews
}
